"app-menu theming" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		App menu
		<header>An app menu is an app's top bar, joined to the top of its window or page: a start section (a menu or side bar button, then a title or breadcrumb), a middle that stays on the bar's centre, and an end section for buttons.</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Set a public `--ui-*` token on the element, any ancestor or `:root`; it inherits into the shadow
			root. Edit a value below to try it.
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-app-menu" playground>
				<ui-app-menu aria-label="Editor demo">
					<ui-item slot="start" icon="magic">
						<ui-text bold>My App</>
					</>
					<ui-item slot="start">File</>
					<ui-item slot="start">Edit</>
					<ui-item slot="start">View</>
					<ui-menu appearance="segmented" aria-label="Mode">
						<ui-item value="run" icon="play">Run</>
						<ui-item value="edit" icon="pencil alternate" selected>Edit</>
					</>
					<ui-item slot="end" link="#settings" icon="cog" aria-label="Settings"></>
					<ui-item slot="end" link="#you" icon="user circle" aria-label="You"></>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  each dresses the bar as it dresses
			its other bars, through `--ui-bar-rest-background` and `--ui-bar-rest-filter`.
		</>
	</>
